Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:03.87,Default,,0,0,0,,So, you're thinking about investing in stocks — and honestly?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.87,0:00:05.03,Default,,0,0,0,,It feels scary.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.03,0:00:06.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Every headline is red.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.57,0:00:11.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Somebody on the internet just lost half their savings on one stock.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.22,0:00:16.24,Default,,0,0,0,,And your brain is doing the maths: what if that happens to me?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.24,0:00:21.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Here's the thing nobody tells you: you're not wrong to feel that way.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.27,0:00:22.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Stocks ARE risky.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.43,0:00:27.07,Default,,0,0,0,,The question is — risky for who, and risky for how long?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.07,0:00:30.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Because the answer changes completely depending on those two things.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.94,0:00:35.97,Default,,0,0,0,,And by the end of this video, you'll know exactly where you stand.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.97,0:00:40.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh — and if you missed part one, go watch it first.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.61,0:00:45.64,Default,,0,0,0,,We covered the three things to do before you touch a single stock.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.64,0:00:47.18,Default,,0,0,0,,This is part two.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.43,0:00:51.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's start with the scary part, because it's real.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.38,0:00:55.76,Default,,0,0,0,,In a single year, the stock market can be brutal.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.76,0:01:00.59,Default,,0,0,0,,The worst year on record, 1931, the market fell almost 44%.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.59,0:01:02.78,Default,,0,0,0,,In 2008, it fell 37%.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.78,0:01:11.98,Default,,0,0,0,,And even in a totally normal year, the market drops about 14% at some point — on average, every single year.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.98,0:01:13.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Wait — what?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.74,0:01:14.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.18,0:01:25.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Since 1980, the market has fallen 14% inside the year, on average — and still ended the year higher in 35 out of 46 years.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.14,0:01:28.64,Default,,0,0,0,,That's the first surprise: the drops are normal.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.64,0:01:33.47,Default,,0,0,0,,They're the price of admission, not a sign that something's broken.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:33.47,0:01:35.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Now here's the second surprise.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:35.66,0:01:38.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Stretch it out, and the picture flips.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:38.73,0:01:47.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Since 1928 — that's almost a hundred years — the stock market has averaged about 10% a year, with dividends reinvested.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:47.93,0:01:54.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Through wars, recessions, crashes, pandemics — all of it — about 10% a year.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:54.07,0:02:01.52,Default,,0,0,0,,But — and this is the important bit — almost no single year actually gives you 10%.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:01.52,0:02:05.47,Default,,0,0,0,,The best year ever was 1954: up nearly 53%.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.47,0:02:08.10,Default,,0,0,0,,The worst was 1931: down 44%.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:08.10,0:02:14.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Saying stocks return 10% a year is like saying the average rollercoaster is 10% scary.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.68,0:02:18.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Technically true — completely useless when you're upside down.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:18.62,0:02:24.32,Default,,0,0,0,,So the average is real, but you never actually experience the average.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.32,0:02:26.07,Default,,0,0,0,,You experience the ride.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:26.32,0:02:30.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, part two of the fear: what if I pick the wrong one?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.79,0:02:38.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Fair question — because if you put all your money in ONE company, and that company goes bust, you can lose everything.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.34,0:02:39.37,Default,,0,0,0,,It has happened.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.37,0:02:40.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Big names, gone.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:40.40,0:02:42.46,Default,,0,0,0,,That is not a small risk.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:42.46,0:02:44.17,Default,,0,0,0,,That is a huge risk.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.17,0:02:48.29,Default,,0,0,0,,But here's the trick — you don't have to buy one company.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.29,0:02:51.38,Default,,0,0,0,,An index fund buys hundreds of them at once.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.38,0:02:56.53,Default,,0,0,0,,The S&P 500 is 500 of the biggest companies in America, all in one basket.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:56.53,0:03:00.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Buy the index, and you own a tiny slice of all 500.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.65,0:03:02.71,Default,,0,0,0,,So if one company goes bust?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:02.71,0:03:06.48,Default,,0,0,0,,That's one out of 500 — about 0.2% of your money.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.48,0:03:07.17,Default,,0,0,0,,It stings.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:07.17,0:03:08.54,Default,,0,0,0,,It doesn't sink you.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.54,0:03:10.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Think of it like eggs.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.60,0:03:12.66,Default,,0,0,0,,One egg, dropped — breakfast ruined.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.66,0:03:16.78,Default,,0,0,0,,A basket of 500 eggs, one breaks — you still have breakfast.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.78,0:03:17.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Same money.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.47,0:03:18.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Completely different risk.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.50,0:03:23.30,Default,,0,0,0,,That's the whole idea of an index fund: you're not betting on one horse.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:23.30,0:03:25.36,Default,,0,0,0,,You're betting on the whole racecourse.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.36,0:03:28.80,Default,,0,0,0,,And the racecourse has been running for a hundred years.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.05,0:03:32.10,Default,,0,0,0,,And then there's the biggest lever of all: time.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:32.10,0:03:35.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Here's the number that changed how I think about risk.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:35.49,0:03:39.90,Default,,0,0,0,,In any single year, the market goes up about 73% of the time.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.90,0:03:42.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Roughly three years out of four, you win.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:42.62,0:03:52.80,Default,,0,0,0,,But stretch your holding period to 20 years — and in almost a hundred years of records, there has never been a single 20-year stretch where the market lost money.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.80,0:03:53.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Not one.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:53.48,0:03:57.55,Default,,0,0,0,,The worst 20-year stretch still made about 2 to 3% a year.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:57.55,0:03:59.93,Default,,0,0,0,,The best made almost 18% a year.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.93,0:04:03.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Now — that does not mean the wait is comfortable.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.66,0:04:12.48,Default,,0,0,0,,After the 2008 crash, the market fell 57% — and it took about five and a half years just to get back to where it started.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:12.48,0:04:20.62,Default,,0,0,0,,After the COVID crash in 2020, it fell 34% in about a month — and it was back at new highs in five months.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.62,0:04:21.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Same market.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.30,0:04:23.00,Default,,0,0,0,,One wait was five months.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.00,0:04:24.70,Default,,0,0,0,,The other was five years.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:24.70,0:04:27.07,Default,,0,0,0,,You can't know which one you're getting.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.07,0:04:28.77,Default,,0,0,0,,That's the real risk.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.77,0:04:32.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Not that the market never recovers — it always has, so far.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:32.84,0:04:36.57,Default,,0,0,0,,The risk is that you need the money before it does.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.57,0:04:42.34,Default,,0,0,0,,So the question isn't really "are stocks risky?" The question is "when do I need this money?"
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.59,0:04:45.80,Default,,0,0,0,,So — is investing in stocks too risky for beginners?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.80,0:04:47.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Here's my honest answer.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.09,0:04:52.87,Default,,0,0,0,,If you need this money next year — for rent, for a deposit, for an emergency — yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.87,0:04:53.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Too risky.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.51,0:04:55.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't put it in stocks.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:55.12,0:05:04.75,Default,,0,0,0,,But if this is money you can leave alone for ten, twenty years — and you own the whole basket, not one company — then history says something very different.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.75,0:05:06.04,Default,,0,0,0,,The risk doesn't disappear.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.04,0:05:06.68,Default,,0,0,0,,It shrinks.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.68,0:05:09.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Year by year, the odds tilt in your favour.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.57,0:05:13.10,Default,,0,0,0,,And remember — this is education, not personal financial advice.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.10,0:05:18.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Your situation is your own, so if you're unsure, talk to a licensed adviser in your country.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.56,0:05:21.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Next up — the part you've been waiting for.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:21.77,0:05:23.38,Default,,0,0,0,,How do you actually start?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:23.38,0:05:25.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Which button do you press first?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.31,0:05:27.88,Default,,0,0,0,,That's part three, and it's the simple one.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:27.88,0:05:28.84,Default,,0,0,0,,See you there.
